---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResearchThreads from '../components/ResearchThreads.astro';
import Strip from '../components/Strip.astro';
import Axes from '../components/Axes.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site.js';
import { openSource, adoptedElsewhere, collaborators } from '../data/research.js';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const toolkits = openSource.filter((o) => !o.name.startsWith('Granite'));
---

<Base
  title="Research · Prasanna Sattigeri"
  description="Papers on agents, calibration, attribution and generative modeling, grouped by thread."
  current="research"
>
  <section class="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a> / Research</p>
      <h1>Research</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The papers, grouped by thread: agents, calibration and attribution, which feed{' '}
        <a href={`${base}/granite-guardian/`}>Granite Guardian</a> and the{' '}
        <a href={`${base}/granite-switch/`}>Granite Switch</a>, and the generative modeling before them. The full
        list is under <a href={`${base}/publications/`}>Publications</a> and on <a href={links.scholar}>Google Scholar</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="agents">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Agents and post-training</p>
        <h2>Agents, calibration and attribution</h2>
      </div>
      <h3 class="sub-h first">Featured · COLM 2026</h3>
      <article class="card feature">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <h3>
            <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.04373">Decocted Experience: context as a second axis for scaling agents</a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Test-time scaling means more compute: longer reasoning, more samples, more search. For agents much of that
            is spent exploring paths that go nowhere. This paper asks what happens if you scale the input instead and
            build the agent’s context from its own past runs.
          </p>
          <p>
            Three results. Lessons distilled from experience beat raw experience and keep scaling as context grows.
            Memory has a sweet spot; an intermediate size beats keeping everything. And context with higher information
            gain about the output gives more efficient inference, which in practice means balancing relevance against
            diversity. Validated on math, web shopping and software engineering agents, with Maohao Shen, Kaiwen Zha,
            Zexue He and Gregory Wornell among others.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Axes />
      </article>

      <h3 class="sub-h">The papers</h3>
      <ResearchThreads only={['agents', 'uncertainty', 'attribution']} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="generative">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Generative modeling</p>
        <h2>A decade of generative models</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Before LLMs I worked on what a generative model learns and how to control it. The same questions now show up
          as synthetic data: what to generate so that a judge learns the right thing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Strip />
      <p class="fine">
        DIP-VAE is one of the six methods in the ICML 2019 best paper by Locatello et al., which trained more than 12,000
        disentanglement models. It is implemented in{' '}
        {adoptedElsewhere.map((o, i) => (
          <>
            <a href={o.url}>{o.name}</a>
            {i < adoptedElsewhere.length - 1 ? ' and ' : '.'}
          </>
        ))}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="research">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
        <h2>Other threads</h2>
      </div>
      <ResearchThreads only={['human-ai', 'foundations']} />
      <h3 class="sub-h">Toolkits</h3>
      <ul class="oss">
        {
          toolkits.map((o) => (
            <li>
              <p class="oss-name">
                <a href={o.url}>{o.name}</a>
              </p>
              <p class="oss-what">
                {o.what} <span class="oss-role">{o.role}.</span>
              </p>
              <p class="oss-adoption">{o.adoption}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="collaborations">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Collaborations</p>
        <h2>Academic collaborations and service</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="collab">
        {
          collaborators.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <p class="place">{c.place}</p>
              <p class="people">
                {c.people}
                {c.with && <span class="with">; with {c.with}</span>}
              </p>
              <p class="topics">{c.topics}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="fine">Affiliations as on the joint papers.</p>
      <h3 class="sub-h">Joint projects</h3>
      <p>
        Principal investigator on two MIT-IBM Watson AI Lab projects, trustworthy learning with limited data with
        Gregory Wornell and human-centric AI for shared decisions with David Sontag, and on joint work with RPI on
        causal inference and agent safety with Ali Tajer and Mohammad Mohammadi Amiri. The MIT projects produced
        Thermometer, the EDL paper, the COLM paper, and the learning-to-defer and onboarding papers.
      </p>
      <h3 class="sub-h">Mentoring</h3>
      <p>
        Thesis committees for Joshua Lee and Maohao Shen at MIT and Burak Varıcı at RPI. Interns most years for a
        decade; two of the 2026 papers above started as internships.
      </p>
      <h3 class="sub-h">Service</h3>
      <ul class="plain two-col">
        <li>Associate Editor, Pattern Recognition</li>
        <li>Area chair and senior PC: NeurIPS, ICML, ICLR, AAAI</li>
        <li>IEEE Senior Member</li>
        <li>Invited talks at the National Academy of Sciences, the MIT AI Conference and NAACL TrustNLP (2024)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .top {
    padding-block: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px) clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  .top .eyebrow a {
    color: inherit;
  }
  .top h1 {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px) clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px);
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(180px, 240px);
    gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 72px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .hero :global(.photo) {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 34px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 17ch;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .hero .lede {
    max-width: 72ch;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .pillars {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .pillar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 22px 24px 0 0;
  }
  .pillar + .pillar {
    padding-left: 24px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .pillar h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .pillar h2 a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .pillar-body {
    margin: 10px 0 16px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .pillar dl {
    margin: auto 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .pillar dl div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .pillar dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .pillar dt {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .band {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    margin: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px) 0 0;
    padding: 18px 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .band div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 4px;
    padding-right: 20px;
  }
  .band dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .band dt {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .embed {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .embed iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 740px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #121619;
  }
  .embed figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .embed iframe {
      display: none;
    }
  }
  .sub-h {
    margin: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px) 0 18px;
  }
  .sub-h.first {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  #collaborations .wrap > p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 90ch;
  }
  .fine {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    max-width: 90ch;
  }

  .yr-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .yr-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding-block: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .yr-list li > span:first-child {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .yr-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .lead-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px) clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px);
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
  }
  .lead-grid p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .lead-grid h3 + p + h3 {
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  .how {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 56px);
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .how p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .code {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .beyond {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px);
  }
  .fact {
    padding: 18px;
  }
  .fact p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .fact-head {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .fact-value {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 6px 0 !important;
  }
  .fact-body {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .shot {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
  }
  .shot > a {
    display: block;
    padding: clamp(12px, 2.4vw, 24px);
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .charts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .caps td {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    padding-block: 10px;
  }
  .caps td:first-child {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    min-width: 170px;
  }
  .caps td:nth-child(2) {
    min-width: 200px;
  }
  .caps td:nth-child(3) {
    min-width: 240px;
  }

  .feature {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .feature h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem);
  }
  .feature h3 a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .feature-text p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .quotes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .quote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.14rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .quote figcaption {
    margin-top: auto;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .use-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 3vw, 40px);
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .usage {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 20px 24px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .usage div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .usage dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .usage dt {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .adoption {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 3vw, 40px);
    margin-top: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
  }
  .adoption h3 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .adoption .plain {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .adoption a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .adoption a:hover {
    color: var(--link);
  }
  .plain {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .two-col {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px);
  }

  .oss {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .oss li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: 6px 28px;
    padding-block: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .oss p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .oss-name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .oss-name a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .oss-what {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .oss-role {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .oss-adoption {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .collab {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px);
  }
  .collab li {
    padding-block: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .collab p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .place {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .people {
    margin-top: 2px !important;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .with {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .topics {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .pillars {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .pillar,
    .pillar + .pillar {
      padding: 20px 0;
      border-left: 0;
    }
    .pillar + .pillar {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .band,
    .usage {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
    .band {
      row-gap: 16px;
    }
    .lead-grid,
    .how,
    .beyond,
    .charts,
    .feature,
    .quotes,
    .use-grid,
    .adoption,
    .collab,
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .oss li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .hero :global(.photo) {
      width: 104px;
      order: -1;
      border-radius: 12px;
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
